-- Up
--
-- Retire the legacy per-message `message_reads` table.
--
-- Precondition: `CHAT_LEGACY_READS_ENABLED` is set to `false` across every
-- running instance for at least one full release cycle, and
-- `chat_read_watermarks` has been proven to be the sole source of truth
-- for unread-count queries. `countUnreadMessages` already prefers the
-- watermark when it exists; after the flag flip, every active user will
-- have a watermark row on their first MARK_READ and the fallback LEFT
-- JOIN path in `countUnreadMessages` becomes unreachable.
--
-- STATUS: **pending** — this file uses the `.sql.pending` extension so the
-- runtime auto-apply migration runner skips it. When the team is ready to
-- execute the cutover, rename the file to `.sql` in a separate PR so the
-- change lands deliberately and reviewers can confirm the preconditions.
--
-- Rollback note: dropping this table is destructive. There is no "Down"
-- path — the per-message read history is not reconstructible from the
-- watermark alone. If this is a concern, snapshot the table into cold
-- storage before enabling the migration.

DROP INDEX IF EXISTS idx_message_reads_user;
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS message_reads;
